<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <ScenarioDef ParentName="ScenarioBase">
    <defName>Archinity_SeedOfArchinity</defName>
    <label>Seed of Archinity</label>
    <description>Your tribe knows fire, stone, and the two who cannot die.\n\nThey were born among you and they never grew old. They bleed and close. They drown and stand back up. They will not eat what you eat.\n\nThe elders say the sky-things made them as a message. Nobody can read it yet.\n\nNote: you start at the absolute bottom of the technology tree with two immensely powerful but permanently unstable colonists who require human blood. This is a very long game.</description>
    <scenario>
      <summary>A neolithic tribe carrying two archite-tainted immortals, at the very beginning of everything.</summary>
      <playerFaction>
        <factionDef>PlayerTribe</factionDef>
      </playerFaction>
      <parts>

        <!-- Config pages: 2 archonians + 2 baseliners = 4 starting pawns -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_ConfigPage_ConfigureStartingPawns_Xenotypes">
          <def>ConfigurePawnsXenotypes</def>
          <pawnChoiceCount>10</pawnChoiceCount>
          <customSummary>Start with two adult archonian sanguophages and two ordinary tribespeople.</customSummary>
          <xenotypeCounts>
            <li>
              <xenotype>Archinity_ArchonianSanguophage</xenotype>
              <count>2</count>
              <description>adult archonian sanguophage</description>
              <requiredAtStart>true</requiredAtStart>
              <allowedDevelopmentalStages>Adult</allowedDevelopmentalStages>
            </li>
            <li>
              <xenotype>Baseliner</xenotype>
              <count>2</count>
            </li>
          </xenotypeCounts>
        </li>

        <!-- Arrival -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_PlayerPawnsArriveMethod">
          <def>PlayerPawnsArriveMethod</def>
          <method>Standing</method>
        </li>

        <!-- Game start dialog -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_GameStartDialog">
          <def>GameStartDialog</def>
          <text>Your people have walked a long way from the burned place.\n\nFour of you are left. Two who bleed properly, and two who do not.\n\nThe two do not remember being born. They do not remember anything before the light in the sky that the elders still refuse to describe. They have buried every person they ever loved and they have not aged a day doing it.\n\nThey are hungry in a way that no animal can fix for long.\n\nHere there is water, stone, and nobody to ask. Build something. The sky-things are watching, and they are further up than anyone can climb.\n\nNot yet.</text>
          <closeSound>GameStartSting</closeSound>
        </li>

        <!-- Starting things: neolithic kit -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>Pemmican</thingDef>
          <count>350</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>MedicineHerbal</thingDef>
          <count>15</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>HemogenPack</thingDef>
          <count>12</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>MeleeWeapon_Club</thingDef>
          <stuff>WoodLog</stuff>
          <count>2</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>MeleeWeapon_Ikwa</thingDef>
          <stuff>Steel</stuff>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>Bow_Short</thingDef>
          <count>2</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingAnimal">
          <def>StartingAnimal</def>
          <count>1</count>
          <bondToRandomPlayerPawnChance>1.0</bondToRandomPlayerPawnChance>
        </li>

        <!-- ================================================================
             THE ALTAR AND THE FIRST VECTOR

             Nothing in the game placed either of these. No quest node, no
             scatterer, no genstep, no recipe. The whole blood mechanic was
             dev spawn only, which is not a start condition, it is an absence.
             The tribe carried the thing here from the burned place: that is
             what the game start text already says happened.

             ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined works for a 3x2 building.
             Decompiled RimWorld.ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined.GenerateThing:
             it calls thing.MakeMinified() whenever thingDef.Minifiable, and
             Verse.ThingDef.Minifiable is minifiedDef != null. Archinity_Altar
             sets minifiedDef MinifiedThing, so what lands in the drop pile is
             a minified crate the colonists install wherever they like. No
             footprint is placed at map gen at all, so
             ScenPart_ScatterThingsNearPlayerStart is not needed and would in
             fact be worse: it would drop the crate at a random nearby cell
             instead of in the starting pile.

             Both entries are guarded on archinity.altar AND on VQE Ancients,
             the comma being the AND form of MayRequire. Both conditions are
             real: the two defs live in Archinity.Altar, which is a separate
             mod and is not currently in the load order, and both are
             themselves MayRequire'd on VQE Ancients, so either mod being
             absent means the def does not exist. Guarded, the ScenParts drop
             silently; unguarded they would be an unresolved cross reference
             on a scenario every start uses.
             ================================================================ -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined" MayRequire="archinity.altar,vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>Archinity_Altar</thingDef>
          <count>1</count>
        </li>
        <!-- The cheap vector: one life, eight hours, and the colony finds out
             what the machine is for. -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined" MayRequire="archinity.altar,vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>Archinity_Vector_PerfectVision</thingDef>
          <count>1</count>
        </li>

        <!-- Scatter -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_ScatterThingsNearPlayerStart">
          <def>ScatterThingsNearPlayerStart</def>
          <thingDef>WoodLog</thingDef>
          <count>400</count>
        </li>

      </parts>
    </scenario>
  </ScenarioDef>

</Defs>
